name: surface-gap
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: a missing verb or surface was discovered by a task that needed it —
  the work routed around the absence and the absence is now named, so the
  next session that greps the module finds the gap already measured.
  Distinct from capability-pinned (a boundary recorded by a test) and
  frontier-red (a wished-for spelling that fails to compile): here the
  green shipped, the gap is a README/concept line, and the signal marks
  that a stdlib surface is smaller than its task.
